{
  "id": "web-dev-111",
  "title": "Interesting Facts About HTML Lists - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>HTML lists are a fundamental part of web development, used to organize and present information in a structured and readable format. While they may seem simple, HTML lists have some interesting features and nuances that make them versatile and powerful.&nbsp;</span></p><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>1.&nbsp;Definition Lists for Metadata</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The&nbsp;</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1749\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>&lt;dl&gt;&nbsp;element</span></a><span> isn’t just for glossaries—it’s ideal for structuring key-value pairs like metadata, settings, or attributes. Each &lt;dt&gt; (term) can have multiple &lt;dd&gt; (descriptions), creating semantic relationships.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dl</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dt</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Author<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dt</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>J.K. Rowling<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dt</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Published<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dt</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>1997<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Bloomsbury (UK)<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dd</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">dl</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>2. CSS Counters for Multi-Level Numbering</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-154\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>CSS counters</span></a><span> (counter-reset,&nbsp;counter-increment) allow custom hierarchical numbering (e.g.,&nbsp;1.1,&nbsp;1.2) in nested lists, overriding default browser behavior.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">counter-reset</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">section</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">list-style</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">none</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"nd\">before</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">counter-increment</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">section</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">content</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">counters</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">section</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\".\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Chapter 1\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n      <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Subsection 1.1<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>3. Override Numbering with&nbsp;</span><code><span>value</span></code></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: start;\"><span>The&nbsp;value&nbsp;attribute in&nbsp;&lt;li&gt;&nbsp;lets you restart or skip numbering mid-list in ordered lists.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 1<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span> <span class=\"na\">value</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"4\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 4 (skipped 2-3)<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 5<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>4.&nbsp;Reverse-Numbered Lists with Semantic Meaning</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The&nbsp;</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1832\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>reversed&nbsp;attribute </span></a><span>in&nbsp;&lt;ol&gt;&nbsp;decrements numbering (e.g., 5, 4, 3) while maintaining semantic order in the DOM. Assistive technologies announce items in visual order.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span> <span class=\"na\">reversed</span> <span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"5\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Phase 5: Launch<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Phase 4: Testing<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>5. Cross-List Number Continuity with&nbsp;</span><code><span>start</span></code></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: start;\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1833\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>&nbsp;start&nbsp;attribute</span></a><span> attribute resumes numbering across separate &lt;ol&gt; elements, mimicking a single continuous list.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span> <span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"3\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Chapter 3<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">&lt;!-- Later in the document --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span> <span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"4\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Chapter 4<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>6.&nbsp;Mid-List Number Override with&nbsp;</span><code><span>value</span></code></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The&nbsp;</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1875\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>value&nbsp;attribute</span></a><span> attribute on &lt;li&gt; forces a specific number, overriding the default sequence. Subsequent items follow the new value.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 1<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span> <span class=\"na\">value</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"10\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 10 (skip ahead)<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Step 11<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"cm\">&lt;!-- Continues from 10 --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>7. Accessible Inline Navigation Menus</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: start;\"><span>Convert vertical lists to horizontal menus using CSS while preserving semantics for screen readers.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nc\">nav-list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">list-style</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">none</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">padding</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">display</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">flex</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">gap</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"kt\">rem</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">style</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ul</span> <span class=\"na\">class</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"nav-list\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span> <span class=\"na\">href</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"/\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Home<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span> <span class=\"na\">href</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"/about\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>About<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ul</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>8.&nbsp;Start Lists at a Specific Number</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The&nbsp;</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1833\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>start&nbsp;attribute</span></a><span> forces ordered lists to begin at a custom number.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span> <span class=\"na\">start</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"5\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Item 5<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Item 6<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ol</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style=\"text-align:left\"><span>9.&nbsp;Shadow DOM List Encapsulation</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Lists inside Shadow DOM components retain their styles without global CSS interference.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">shadow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"nb\">document</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">querySelector</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'#host'</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nx\">attachShadow</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">mode</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'open'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">});</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">shadow</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">innerHTML</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span>\n<span class=\"sb\">    &lt;style&gt;ul { color: blue; }&lt;/style&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"sb\">    &lt;ul&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"sb\">      &lt;li&gt;Isolated list item&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"sb\">    &lt;/ul&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"sb\">  `</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">div</span> <span class=\"na\">id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"host\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">div</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: start;\"><br></p></div>",
  "textContent": "HTML lists are a fundamental part of web development, used to organize and present information in a structured and readable format. While they may seem simple, HTML lists have some interesting features and nuances that make them versatile and powerful. 1. Definition Lists for MetadataThe <dl> element isn’t just for glossaries—it’s ideal for structuring key-value pairs like metadata, settings, or attributes. Each <dt> (term) can have multiple <dd> (descriptions), creating semantic relationships.\n            HTML\n\n    <dl>\n  <dt>Author</dt>\n  <dd>J.K. Rowling</dd>\n  <dt>Published</dt>\n  <dd>1997</dd>\n  <dd>Bloomsbury (UK)</dd>\n</dl>\n\n2. CSS Counters for Multi-Level NumberingCSS counters (counter-reset, counter-increment) allow custom hierarchical numbering (e.g., 1.1, 1.2) in nested lists, overriding default browser behavior.\n            HTML\n\n    <style>\n  ol { counter-reset: section; list-style: none; }\n  li::before { \n    counter-increment: section; \n    content: counters(section, \".\") \" \"; \n  }\n</style>\n<ol>\n  <li>Chapter 1\n    <ol>\n      <li>Subsection 1.1</li>\n    </ol>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n3. Override Numbering with valueThe value attribute in <li> lets you restart or skip numbering mid-list in ordered lists.\n            HTML\n\n    <ol>\n  <li>Step 1</li>\n  <li value=\"4\">Step 4 (skipped 2-3)</li>\n  <li>Step 5</li>\n</ol>\n\n4. Reverse-Numbered Lists with Semantic MeaningThe reversed attribute in <ol> decrements numbering (e.g., 5, 4, 3) while maintaining semantic order in the DOM. Assistive technologies announce items in visual order.\n            HTML\n\n    <ol reversed start=\"5\">\n  <li>Phase 5: Launch</li>\n  <li>Phase 4: Testing</li>\n</ol>\n\n5. Cross-List Number Continuity with startThe start attribute attribute resumes numbering across separate <ol> elements, mimicking a single continuous list.\n            HTML\n\n    <ol start=\"3\">\n  <li>Chapter 3</li>\n</ol>\n<!-- Later in the document -->\n<ol start=\"4\">\n  <li>Chapter 4</li>\n</ol>\n\n6. Mid-List Number Override with valueThe value attribute attribute on <li> forces a specific number, overriding the default sequence. Subsequent items follow the new value.\n            HTML\n\n    <ol>\n  <li>Step 1</li>\n  <li value=\"10\">Step 10 (skip ahead)</li>\n  <li>Step 11</li> <!-- Continues from 10 -->\n</ol>\n\n7. Accessible Inline Navigation MenusConvert vertical lists to horizontal menus using CSS while preserving semantics for screen readers.\n            HTML\n\n    <style>\n  .nav-list {\n    list-style: none;\n    padding: 0;\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 2rem;\n  }\n</style>\n<ul class=\"nav-list\">\n  <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"/about\">About</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n8. Start Lists at a Specific NumberThe start attribute forces ordered lists to begin at a custom number.\n            HTML\n\n    <ol start=\"5\">\n  <li>Item 5</li>\n  <li>Item 6</li>\n</ol>\n\n9. Shadow DOM List EncapsulationLists inside Shadow DOM components retain their styles without global CSS interference.\n            HTML\n\n    <script>\n  const shadow = \ndocument.querySelector('#host').attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });\n  shadow.innerHTML = `\n    <style>ul { color: blue; }</style>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Isolated list item</li>\n    </ul>\n  `;\n</script>\n<div id=\"host\"></div>",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/html/interesting-facts-about-html-lists"
}
